The diff shows the full body of the relevant destructor logic, so it is sufficient to decide. The root cause is that `idxd_conf_device_release()` failed to free the per-device workqueue `idxd->wq`. In this commit, the added destructor is:

`static void idxd_conf_device_release(struct device *dev) {
	struct idxd_device *idxd = container_of(dev, struct idxd_device, conf_dev);

	kfree(idxd->groups);
	kfree(idxd->wqs);
	kfree(idxd->engines);
	kfree(idxd->irq_entries);
	ida_free(idxd_ida(idxd), idxd->id);
	kfree(idxd);
}`

This release function frees several allocations (`groups`, `wqs`, `engines`, `irq_entries`, and finally `idxd`) but does not call any workqueue cleanup such as `destroy_workqueue(idxd->wq)` or otherwise free `idxd->wq`. Since the commit wires this destructor into the top-level device types via:

`struct device_type dsa_device_type = { .release = idxd_conf_device_release, ... };`
`struct device_type iax_device_type = { .release = idxd_conf_device_release, ... };`

and the missing `idxd->wq` cleanup remains absent, the vulnerable construct is present and the fix is not yet included.
